Sentence|Translation
Mes maun è fitg grond|My hand is very big
Nua è tes maun?|Where is your hand?
Has ti in maun?|Do you have a hand?
Mia chomma è pitschna|My leg is small
Mia chomma n'è betg violetta, ella è verd|My leg is not purple, it is green
Jau hai ina chomma e in chau|I have a leg and a head
Nua è tes chau?|Where is your head?
Ha el in chau u in det?|Does he have a head or a finger?
Mes det n'è betg qua|My finger is not here
Ha ella in det?|Does she have a finger?
Jau hai in egl blau|I have a blue eye
Jau hai mo in egl|I only have one eye
Jau hai dus nas, però jau hai mo in egl|I have two noses, but I only have one eye
È mes nas cotschen?|Is my nose red?
In nas e ina bucca|A nose and a mouth
Mia bucca n'è betg gronda|My mouth is not big
Mia bucca è sin tes schanugl|My mouth is on your knee
Jau n'hai betg in schagnul|I don't have a knee
In schagnul, in culiez|A knee, a neck
Mes culiez n'è betg verd|My neck is not green
Jau hai in culiez pitschen|I have a little neck
Mes ravel n'è betg fitg grond|My ankle is not very big
Jau hai om in ravel|I only have one ankle
In ravel u in'ungla?|An ankle or a fingernail?
Mia ungla è fitg gronda|My fingernail is very big
Has ti in'ungla?|Do you have a fingernail?
È mia ungla rosa?|Is my fingernail pink?
Jau hai ina survantscheglia gronda|I have a big eyebrow
Jau hai om ina survantscheglia|I only have one eyebrow
Bainbaud, jau vegn ad avair ina survantscheglia|Soon, I will have an eyebrow